{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 28 (S4 chapter 3, The Far Shores): a quiet green hill country. Wild herders wander the hills (Call brings them in), three wolf dens fill the eastern woods and hunt only the player (beastPrey player), and a weak turtle tribe sits on an isle far to the south east (maxTroops 6, maxPopulation 36; no Boathouse or Skyloft in this level, so neither side can cross to the other and the level bot cannot wipe the rival early: it did by tick 13000 when the rival stood on the mainland, and the night hunters stopped with it). Staged: grow to 30 followers (from 13); clear the three dens of the eastern woods (fromStage clearDens in an area); from minute 6 the moon rises and the far tribe sends two fresh hunters at the Hearth every 45 s until the night ends, and clearing the woods brings three more: survive three minutes from then (survive fromStage; the repeating spawn is bounded by until on it; the engine cannot spawn hunting wolves from a trigger, so the night hunters are rival wardens); dawn sends two new herds of wild herders, grow by 20 more (followers fromStage); then the moon stone wakes on the moon hill to the north east behind a wolf den, the far tribe sends four fresh wardens to stand on the hill (an attack raid, not a pray raid: the level bot cannot strike rival worshippers kneeling at a reliquary, so a pray race stalled it), and six followers pray there (worship fromStage) to finish. Bot win about 19250 (stages at about 5750, 8250, 12000, 16250), time limit 2100 s.",
